1. Click + -> + Create new file

2. Name your file, do not use spaces. End file name with .user.js (example: My_New_Tech_Tool.user.js)

3. Paste all code "Script" into editer

4. Add two new lines in the // ==/UserScript== area

    // @updateURL    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ZRScott/Byte_Sized/main/
    // @downloadURL  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ZRScott/Byte_Sized/main/

   EXAMPLE:
// ==UserScript==
// @name         My New Tech Tool
// @namespace    http://tampermonkey.net/
// @version      1.0
// @match        *://*/*
// @grant        GM_openInTab
// @icon         https://www.svgrepo.com/show/165233/coin.svg
// @updateURL    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ZRScott/Byte_Sized/main/         <---- New row
// @downloadURL  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ZRScott/Byte_Sized/main/         <---- New row
// ==/UserScript==

5. Add your files name to the end of the new lines

      Example:  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ZRScott/Byte_Sized/main/My_New_Tech_Tool.user.js

6. Click Commit Changes...


8. Test out the URL you just made by pasting it into the browser, it should auto-open tampermonkey and ask to install

